Subject: Native entries seal the caller's light frame before running

What this does
  - Every place that calls a unit's native entry (aot_nfn) directly from C (JS_CallInternal, JS_Call, the construct fast path, the Array.prototype.sort comparator call) now seals the current register frame first through regvm_light_seal_out (an out-of-line wrapper, so the hot call paths carry one test and a call), as the other call paths already do.

Why we need it
  A light interpreter frame sits above the arena top until it is sealed. The native entry's step operations (construct, calls) take frames from the arena top, so a frame they allocated overwrote the live light caller. The caller then read its registers back as garbage: a closure variable came out wrong, an inline cache handler ran on a garbage record, and box2d crashed or threw TypeErrors on 'm_flags' and 'm_pointCount' when the hot-cover selection left a constructor compiled and its caller interpreted.

Soundness
  regvm_light_seal only raises the arena top over a frame that is already live; it changes nothing when the frame is already covered and is a no-op without the record call path.

